---
import Layout from "@rpgm/tools-press-theme/components/Layout.astro";
import Prose from "@rpgm/tools-press-theme/components/Prose.astro";
import Flourish from "@rpgm/tools-press-theme/ornaments/Flourish.astro";
import SiteHead from "../components/SiteHead.astro";
import {
  SITE_TITLE,
  SITE_LOGO,
  NAV_LINKS,
  AUTHOR_NAME,
  AUTHOR_AVATAR,
  AUTHOR_GITHUB,
  RPGM_TOOLS_URL,
  REPO_URL,
} from "../consts";
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description={`About ${AUTHOR_NAME}, the person behind ${SITE_TITLE}.`}
  siteTitle={SITE_TITLE}
  logoSrc={SITE_LOGO}
  navLinks={NAV_LINKS}
  rssTitle={SITE_TITLE}
  rssHref="/rss.xml"
  githubHref={REPO_URL}
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <SiteHead />
  </Fragment>

  <p class="rpgm-eyebrow">About</p>
  <div class="about-header">
    <img src={AUTHOR_AVATAR} alt={AUTHOR_NAME} width="96" height="96" class="about-header__avatar" />
    <h1>{AUTHOR_NAME}</h1>
  </div>
  <Flourish size={16} color="var(--rpgm-border-strong)" />

  <Prose>
    <p>
      By day, I lead a marketing data and analytics organization - the kind of
      role where "business intelligence," "data science," and, these days,
      "AI" all show up in the same sentence more often than not. I got there
      by a slightly winding path: a bachelor's in information technology,
      over a decade in marketing analytics roles of increasing scope, then an
      MBA and a master's in business analytics along the way. I've also spent
      the last several years teaching as an adjunct professor - mostly
      technology, analytics, and business courses - because explaining
      something well is usually the fastest way to find out whether you
      actually understand it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Software engineering is the newest chapter here, not the oldest. I've
      been writing real code seriously for only a few years - though if you
      count the fifteen years I spent running my own small Apple repair and
      training business before that, "comfortable pulling a computer apart"
      isn't new to me, just "shipping software" is. What's genuinely new is
      doing it with AI as a constant working partner rather than an
      occasional assist - that's most of how RPGM Tools, and this blog
      itself, actually get built day to day.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href={RPGM_TOOLS_URL}>RPGM Tools</a> is where the rest of my time
      goes: I'm the principal and co-founder, building a small suite of
      AI-driven tools for the tabletop RPG community, including Neo Angband, a
      from-scratch port of a roguelike that's been in continuous development
      since 1990. <em>Relics &amp; Reckonings</em> is the notebook that comes
      out of all of it - the relics I've built on purpose, and the reckonings
      I only understood after the fact.
    </p>
    <p>
      Elsewhere: <a href={AUTHOR_GITHUB}>GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--rpgm-space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--rpgm-space-4);
  }

  .about-header h1 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .about-header__avatar {
    border-radius: var(--rpgm-radius-full);
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 1px solid var(--rpgm-border-strong);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
</style>
